title: CompoundFieldHeaders
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

A sub-entry of a `text/vnd.tiddlywiki-multiple+fields` tiddler can carry presentation headers next to its `type:`. They are read through the `compound-field-meta` operator, so a template named in [[inherit-compound|InheritCompoundField]] sets them once for every record.

|!Header |!Effect |
|`label` |caption shown instead of the field name |
|`tooltip` |`title` attribute on the caption |
|`placeholder` |placeholder of the text input or textarea |
|`hide-filter` |a filter; when it returns anything the field is left out of `compound-field-names:visible[]` |
|`readonly-filter` |a filter; when it returns anything the field renders in view mode even where edit mode was requested |

Both filters run with `currentTiddler` set to the record, so start them from `<currentTiddler>` or a `{!!field}` reference.

```
title: list
type: relation-Company
label: Company
+
title: email
type: email
placeholder: name@example.com
+
title: notes
type: multiline
hide-filter: [{!!category}match[personal]]
+
title: birthday
type: date
readonly-filter: [{!!category}match[business]]
```

! The compound-field procedure

`$:/core/macros/compound-field` defines two procedures for view and edit templates:

* `<<compound-field fieldName="…" mode="…" type="…">>` renders one field. `mode` is `view` (default) or `edit`. `type` overrides the sub-entry's `type:` header. On a tiddler that is not a compound tiddler it is the only source of the type; without it the field renders as single-line text
* `<<compound-field-label fieldName>>` renders the caption, honouring `label` and `tooltip`

On a `+fields` tiddler the control writes the sub-entry. On any other tiddler it writes the named field, so the same call works in a template for standard tiddlers:

```
<table>
<tr><td><<compound-field-label "email">></td><td><<compound-field fieldName="email" mode="edit" type="email">></td></tr>
<tr><td>Born</td><td><<compound-field fieldName="birthday" mode="edit" type="date">></td></tr>
</table>
```

A custom template lists the fields a record shows with `[<currentTiddler>compound-field-names:visible[]]`. The core edit template lists every field on purpose, so a hidden field stays reachable there, and its raw text mode is not affected by `readonly-filter`.

! Operator forms

* `[<T>compound-field-meta:KEY<name>]` reads header `KEY` of sub-entry `name`. The operand form `compound-field-meta[name::KEY]` still works and is needed when `KEY` itself comes from a variable, as the `select-` editor does
* `[<T>compound-field-names:visible[]]` is `compound-field-names[]` minus the entries whose `hide-filter` matches
